␀␀How tiles work:
The map is built from 256Г—256 "slippy" tiles. Only the tiles for the area you're viewing are fetched вЂ” there is no bulk pre-download.

Because this device can't do HTTPS (not enough heap after Wi-Fi starts) and decodes JPEG far more cheaply than PNG, tiles come from the wadamesh proxy: it fetches the upstream PNG over HTTPS with an identifying User-Agent, re-encodes it as JPEG, and caches it. Your device then caches each tile to its own flash, so a tile is only downloaded once.

